# ---- yours: never commit ----
# Everything of yours, under one roof: every conversation, what each persona
# remembers about you, what each room has become, what this machine is tuned
# to, and the TLS keys that let your phone reach it.
#
# One line on purpose, and it stays one line: anything private invented later
# goes under here rather than beside the code. See machine/paths.py.
/userdata/

# ---- the models ----
# Twelve gigabytes of weights that belong to whoever published them, downloaded
# by setup.sh and kept beside the code so the whole thing is one directory you
# can move or delete. Never ours to commit.
/models/

# ---- the voices ----
# A reference clip is six seconds of somebody's actual voice, and it is the one
# asset here that cannot be taken back once it is published. So none of them
# live in git: setup.sh fetches the pack onto the shelf at models/voices/,
# which the line above already covers. This one stays for a clip left lying
# where they used to live, beside a character -- a clip contributed in a pull
# request has nowhere to land, which is a guarantee rather than something a
# reviewer has to catch on a tired afternoon. See THIRD-PARTY.md.
voice.ref.wav

# ---- the app package ----
# Installed, built and reported: every one of these is produced by a command in
# app/package.json and none of it is anybody's work. The lockfile is, and stays.
node_modules
app/dist/
app/playwright-report/
test-results/

# ---- the lab ----
# Benches, scorers and the baseline snapshotter: scripts for measuring this
# machine and this checkout, run by hand while working on the code. They are
# not part of the program and are never published; what they measured is
# written into the code beside the number it justified.
/lab/

# ---- machine-local ----
# a sink at the root: scratch tools, logs, anything mid-experiment. Nothing
# in the program reads it, and nothing in it is expected to survive.
/tmp/
# browser screenshots taken while designing the pages
/.playwright-mcp/
.venv/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store

# ---- working notes ----
# Plans and notes written while working on the code are not part of it.
PLAN-*.md
